join Lebo (Neutral) left
join Hope (Neutral) right
update Lebo (Warm)
- Someone mentioned a pathway?
	Hope: Someone mentioned a pathway?
	Lebo: Ah, they told you. Of course they told you, they tell everyone, it's the first thing anyone says about me —
	Lebo: Right, so, the low track washes out every year, and I thought, that's easy, that's just fill and a bit of gravel and a lip to hold it. Half a day. Did it in an afternoon.
	Lebo: And Amos comes and looks at it. Doesn't say anything for about a minute. Then he says — 'water still has to go somewhere.'
	Lebo: And I said yes, obviously, and he said 'where,' and I said —
	Lebo: I hadn't thought about where.
	Lebo: It lasted nine days! Nine! There's a hole there now that's bigger than the one I filled in.
	Lebo: He's never mentioned it again. Not once. That's worse, somehow.
